fact WorkItem(id: "WI-837", description: some(value: "A WI-450 witness-supplied `eq` never keys the semantic-equality dispatch index, so a carrier whose PartialEq is provided by a WITNESS SORT silently answers STRUCTURAL equality. The index build (rustland/anthill-core/src/kb/load.rs:4805-4815, WI-616 pass 3) takes `carrier_own_op(kb, sort, PartialEq.eq, eq).or_else(|| instance_fact_eq_target(...))` — the carrier's own member, else a CARRIER-KEYED instance fact. A provision whose `sort_ref` is the WITNESS (`sort MyEq { fact PartialEq[T = Pebble]  operation eq(a: Pebble, b: Pebble) -> Bool = … }`) is keyed on the witness, not the carrier, so it is invisible to that walk. The asymmetry is already known and bridged on the OTHER dispatch path — `witness_provision` / `witness_op_for_carrier` (kb/typing.rs:16116, :16164) exist precisely for `sort_ref != carrier` — but semantic eq/neq does NOT go through them: resolver and interpreter both probe `sem_eq_dispatch_target` only (resolve/*.rs eq/neq builtin; eval/builtins.rs:549), which reads the index. TODAY this is a silent DEGRADATION (the witness's `eq` is ignored and structural equality answers). It becomes a SOUNDNESS GATE for docs/proposals/058-modular-instances.md phase 3b (WI-648): 3b deletes the load-time `AmbiguousWitness` refusal (kb/typing.rs:~15995, which is spec-generic and is currently the ONLY thing rejecting two witness-sort PartialEq providers for one carrier), and 058 §4.9's hardening refuses a second candidate AT THE INDEX BUILD — but no witness ever reaches the index, so two Eq witnesses would coexist with no diagnostic from either check and equality would silently go structural. 058 §6's claim that the Eq family keeps load-time coherence 'by mechanism, not accident' is FALSE for the witness form until this is closed; 058 §4.9 currently mis-files this as an independent candidate ticket rather than a phase-3a prerequisite. SIBLING BLIND SPOTS from the same audit (fix together or file separately): a first SortProvidesInfo fact that binds no `eq` hides a second that does (provider_spec_view_bindings early-returns at kb/typing.rs:18229), silently degrading to structural eq; the eval bridge's `BridgeRequirements::Unresolvable` outcome is trace-only (eval/eval.rs:1785). ACCEPTANCE: a carrier whose ONLY PartialEq provider is a witness sort dispatches `eq` to the witness's member — test with a witness `eq` whose answer is deliberately NON-structural, observed by BOTH the resolver and the interpreter; the index build refuses a second candidate for one carrier at LOAD, naming both providers; the existing carrier-own-op and instance-fact paths are unchanged (their tests stay green); full workspace green via rustland/scripts/test.sh."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-29T11:35:10Z"))

